> Nobody yet tried and succeeded with an extinctionist in SporkHack?

Not even close.  You're welcome to try though -- it'd be interesting to
see whether it's even practical to do anymore.  A lot of things I
haven't worried about too much yet because people have been more focused
on (as Tenaya noted) "crap -- I need to win".  I figure eventually
people will get used to the tougher endgame and start exploring other
possibilities.  I know someone was trying a pacifist for awhile and left
scads of bones all over the dungeon as a result; this is fabulous, in my
opinion, because conducts aren't _inherently_ bad as long as the game
itself played without conducts is also reasonably challenging.  If
conducts happen to become hard enough such that individual ones are a
major achievement, so much the better.

> Does the changed monster generation depending on the turn counter
